<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nnamdi Azikiwe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1904–1996</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nnamdi Azikiwe, known as Zik, was a leading Nigerian nationalist and journalist and the first President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. Through his newspapers, starting with the West African Pilot in 1937, and the National Council of Nigeria and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroons</a>, he campaigned for independence. He was premier of the Eastern Region, governor-general from 1960 and president of the republic from 1963 until the military coup of 1966.</p></div>
